# One image, one placement

Do not use the same image twice in a book.

The only intended exception is a cover image that also appears inside the book (title page, chapter opener, or similar). That is branding the edition, not filling pages.

When placing, keeping, or fetching images:

- If a file is already used in that book’s `src/`, skip it. Same photo under a different filename or path still counts as a duplicate.
- A wiki dump that repeats a photo across chapters should keep one placement and drop the rest.
- Do not “fill” a chapter with a photo already used elsewhere in the same title.
